+# NativeDate source registration successor
+
+Subject b423c0e0b754b1f1d118d17e022981c357c3aa68; basis 9a5fac0b285f5663d1b8e00f9df3ef34b7c26a4c. This source-only successor preserves the 4903 registration and its earlier reviews by a hash-bound prior evidence record. It supplies no security, floor, clean coordinator execution or G11 qualification. The complete packed106 and both rich observations remain mandatory in a clean current same-library coordinator run.
+
+Of the 18 registered source members, sixteen match the previous registration. The two changed complete source comparisons from 4903 to 9a5 are:
+
+* The shared audit checker imports `tableOutputRecords`, appends its records to the existing datepicker live output list, and uses a general inherited-evidence mismatch error. The existing loop still reads each output and verifies byte length and SHA-256 before acceptance; the NativeDate dispatch, reader and individual scope are unchanged. The table producer/sealer and shared checker closure require their own coordinator qualification, which this review does not provide.
+* The full-verify matrix adds twelve historical artifact IDs: two option, two input, four select, two table, one tab-header and one tooltip. No existing matrix lines were removed or changed. Both NativeDate case IDs remain present exactly once. These additions are required coverage, not evidence of execution.
+
+The other three members that changed relative to the original registration (packed evidence, packed producer, and public API), and the earlier checker and matrix changes, remain covered by the prior 4903 source review. The owned adapter, module, Material 16 reference, NativeDate fixture, predicates, and evidence reader are unchanged. The d70 packed106 observations were from a dirty iteration and do not substitute for the required clean coordinator run.
